{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1564539-curseborne-covenant-is-now-on-kickstarter","id":1564539,"title":"Curseborne Covenant is NOW ON KICKSTARTER!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-10-05T09:29:53-07:00","id":1564539,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon4.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Curseborne Covenant is NOW ON KICKSTARTER!","content":"<b><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/curseborne-covenant\" target=\"_blank\">Curseborne Covenant</a></b> introduces a new group for the characters to ally themselves with: the conspiracy. These formidable factions eat away at the fabric of Accursed community, a secret wrapped within a secret. They\u2019re a way for elder Accursed to while away the years, grow their own powerbase, control the \u201clesser\u201d Accursed, and spread their own particular brand of curse. While some conspiracies have lofty goals, others are decidedly less altruistic in their pursuits. The rest, well, they make the others seem like saints by comparison.<br /> <br /> Conspiracies are central to <b><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/curseborne-covenant\" target=\"_blank\">Curseborne Covenant</a></b>\u200b, and each one represents a mystery deeper than any the world of Curseborne has explored so far. Each conspiracy acts as both a moral imperative and a social group for a character to attach themselves to. By pursuing these routes, the characters get to explore their own rapidly expanding worldview and start pulling the strings themselves. Doing so allows them to unlock the real power behind their curse, placing them into a whole new level. <a href=\"filedata/fetch?id=1564540&amp;d=1791217038&amp;type=thumb\" title=\"Click image for larger version Name: Covenant Splash QR_2.png Views: 179 Size: 251.6 KB ID: 1564540\" >Covenant Splash QR_2.png</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <b><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/curseborne-covenant\" target=\"_blank\">Curseborne Covenant</a></b>\u200b is the next major expansion for <b>Curseborne</b>, Onyx Path Publishing's tabletop roleplaying game of contemporary urban horror using the Storypath Ultra system.\u200b<br /> <br /> Inside the full-color hardcover book, you will find:<ul><li><b>Chapter One: The Tattered World</b>. We begin with our setting chapter. This is still the same cursed world you\u2019re accustomed to, and this chapter just brings things up to speed in terms of what developments you\u2019re going to want to bring in.</li> <li><b>Chapter Two: Enter the Conspiracy</b>. This chapter dives straight into the conspiracies, giving an Accursed eye view of what they are and what they do. Each conspiracy receives a detailed write-up as to their objectives and beliefs, as well as what joining one offers the characters.</li> <li><b>Chapter Three: Families</b>. Curseborne Covenant offers up five new Families; one for each Lineage. Importantly, each of these Families has a direct connection to the Fae. Here you\u2019ll find some guidance as to how our high Entanglement characters might found a new Family of their own.</li> <li><b>Chapter Four: Character Advancement</b>.For all things character advancement, look no further than chapter 4. New Inheritances, Motifs, Damnations, Edges, Relics, Heirlooms, and even advice for those wanting to switch their Major Path over.</li> <li><b>Chapter Five: Curses</b>. If you want mechanics for how to cursebind, details on the new rituals created by the conspiracies, and the insidious power behind the new ascendant spells, this chapter is where you need to go.</li> <li><b>Chapter Six: Conspiracy and Control</b>.This is our Storyguiding chapter, giving you guidance and advice on how to weave these new elements into your stories. You\u2019ll uncover a huge range of inspirational material here too, giving you some ready-made story starting points. With all this power at your fingertips, the characters are going to need some equally potent adversaries to keep them busy. You\u2019ll also find them in this chapter!</li> </ul>Follow the moth and back <b>\u200b<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/curseborne-covenant\" target=\"_blank\">Curseborne Covenant</a></b> on Kickstarter at <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/curseborne-covenant\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.kickstarter.com/projects...borne-covenant</a><br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}